      "title": "How it works",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "8.0.1",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "1. Paste the full path of a GIF into the path box. GIF Optimise has its own gif picker for files in the input folder, but the path box lets the compare node see the original too.\n2. GIF Optimise re-encodes it (mode smallest here; try target_size with target_size_mb for a size budget).\n3. GIF Analyse / Compare measures both GIFs and shows them side by side, split or as a difference image. The report gives sizes, frame counts and SSIM and PSNR, so you can see what the saving cost in quality."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "1. Paste the full path of a GIF into the path box. GIF Optimise has its own gif picker for files in the input folder, but the path box lets the compare node see the original too.\n2. GIF Optimise re-encodes it (mode smallest here; try target_size with target_size_mb for a size budget).\n3. GIF Analyse / Compare measures both GIFs and shows them side by side, split or as a difference image. The report gives sizes, frame counts and SSIM and PSNR, so you can see what the saving cost in quality."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
